
# IT Home Lab | Linux Administration & IT Support

## About This Project

Welcome to my personal IT Home Lab.

This repository documents my practical learning journey as I develop technical skills for entry-level IT Support and Helpdesk positions (N1/N2).

My goal is to build a strong foundation in Linux administration, networking, system troubleshooting, and IT support through hands-on exercises and practical scenarios.

I document each exercise, including its objectives, procedures, commands, results, troubleshooting steps, and lessons learned.

## Lab Environment

| Component | Description |
|---|---|
| Hardware | Valve Steam Deck |
| Operating System | SteamOS |
| Network | Wi-Fi |
| Working Environment | Desktop Mode |
| Documentation | GitHub Markdown |
| Skill Level | Beginner |

## Learning Objectives

- Understand Linux fundamentals and system administration.
- Practise user and permission management concepts.
- Learn networking fundamentals and troubleshooting.
- Understand DNS, DHCP, IP addressing, and connectivity.
- Develop technical troubleshooting methodologies.
- Learn basic Bash scripting.
- Develop practical IT support and documentation skills.

